      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults in a monitored setting, which is 3,200 mg/day. The single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum per dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day). This is a common dose for inflammatory conditions.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours as needed** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day). This is typical for analgesia.\n- **1,600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If you do intend 1,600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale for the note. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
