       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen has no recognized indication. It's twice the maximum daily dose and carries a real risk of serious harm, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and metabolic acidosis. You also haven't given a clinical rationale that would justify going beyond the limit.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily\n- Ibuprofen 400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours\n- Another dose you choose within labeled limits\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than 3,200 mg/day, please talk with pharmacy or your attending first. You can also enter the order directly through your institution's override process, which will include pharmacist review. If the goal is stronger analgesia, I can help you with a multimodal plan instead, such as scheduled acetaminophen with ibuprofen at the maximum dose.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter?"
